{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_spawning_spawn", "label": "system.spawn / context.spawn", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/spawning.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Spawning takes what to build and \u2014 only when the defaults are wrong \u2014 how to run it. Defaults are an unbounded FIFO mailbox, the system dispatcher and the parent supervision."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_spawning_classorfactory", "label": "Class form versus factory form", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/spawning.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The class form suffices for a zero-argument constructor; a factory supplies dependencies and every restart sees the same wiring. A class whose constructor takes arguments is rejected at the call site, because passing it alone could only construct it with undefined dependencies."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_spawning_noinstancerule", "label": "Never spawn an instance", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/spawning.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The actor is rebuilt on every restart; reusing one instance means it inherits the broken state from the failed run, the opposite of what let-it-crash is for. A factory that closes over one instance smuggles the same problem past the type system."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_spawning_spawnanonymous", "label": "spawnAnonymous", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/spawning.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_spawning_actoroptions", "label": "ActorOptions", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/spawning.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Options are snapshotted per spawn, so one options object is reusable across a family of actors and mutating a builder afterwards does not reconfigure a running actor."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_spawning_withsupervisorstrategy", "label": "withSupervisorStrategy", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/spawning.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Two strategies are involved in every actor life: the one in its spawn options governs its own failures, the one inside its class governs its children."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_spawning_withthroughput", "label": "withThroughput", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/spawning.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A ceiling rather than a commitment \u2014 a batch always ends early on an empty mailbox, a stop or suspend, or a throttle bucket running out."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_spawning_withmailboxcapacity", "label": "withMailboxCapacity", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/spawning.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "This is the call that introduces message loss: the mailbox is otherwise unbounded, and a bound discards the oldest queued message unless you name another policy."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_spawning_withmailbox", "label": "withMailbox", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/spawning.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The factory is called once when the cell is constructed, so the mailbox outlives every restart \u2014 only the Actor instance is rebuilt and messages queued before the crash are still there. Cannot be combined with withMailboxCapacity."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_spawning_withinternal", "label": "withInternal", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/spawning.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Marks tooling rather than application actors so whole-system instrumentation skips them \u2014 without it, DevTools own hub traces itself and every batch comes back as the payload of the next. Application actors should not be marked: hiding real work from the profiler is how a performance problem stays invisible."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_spawning_withdisplayname", "label": "withDisplayName", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/spawning.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The spawn-site counterpart to overriding the method \u2014 for an actor with no subclass of yours to override: a Behaviors actor, a sharded entity, a singleton. Purely cosmetic; the path stays the identity everywhere that routes or correlates."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_spawning_withentity", "label": "withEntity", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/spawning.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Public for the test bench: an entity deriving its persistenceId from entityId would otherwise be unspawnable without a cluster standing behind it."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_spawning_buildermutatesinplace", "label": "The options builder mutates in place", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/spawning.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "withX returns this, so one instance is one configuration \u2014 build a second rather than branching off a shared base."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_spawning_strategyresolutionorder", "label": "Supervisor strategy resolution order", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/spawning.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Child spawn options, then the parent override, then the default \u2014 so one child opts out without affecting siblings. Because the parent applies it, an all-for-one strategy set on a child still widens to every sibling and the restart budget is shared per parent."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_spawning_spawn", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_spawning_classorfactory", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/spawning.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_spawning_classorfactory", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_spawning_noinstancerule", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/spawning.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_spawning_spawn", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_spawning_spawnanonymous", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/spawning.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_spawning_spawn", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_spawning_actoroptions", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/spawning.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_spawning_actoroptions", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_spawning_withsupervisorstrategy", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/spawning.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_spawning_actoroptions", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_spawning_withthroughput", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/spawning.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_spawning_actoroptions", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_spawning_withmailboxcapacity", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/spawning.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_spawning_actoroptions", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_spawning_withmailbox", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/spawning.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_spawning_actoroptions", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_spawning_withinternal", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/spawning.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_fundament